WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:06.790
Speaker 1: A bunch of you sent me articles
about this next story.

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:12.200
And it shouldn't come as a surprise, but it
should be extraordinarily alarming because

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.929
of what it means.

00:00:13.929 --> 00:00:21.360
The accounting firm, which has represented
Trump's business for a decade, is now saying,

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:25.100
We can't trust, you can't trust I me David
Pakman.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:33.230
I can't trust the financial accounting records
that they put together for the last decade

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:38.680
because they may be based on underlying fraudulent
information.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:44.520
And the accounting firm has abandoned Trump
and says they will no longer represent Trump's

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:45.520
business.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.520
This is unbelievable.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:53.000
A Yahoo News, NBC News reporting Trump Organization's
accounting firms says.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:59.010
Accounting firm says it can no longer vouch
for financial statements from the company.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:03.970
This is a major story, and it is not getting
the attention it deserves.

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:12.850
The accounting firm Mazars USA said a decade's
worth of financial statements from the Trump

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:15.740
Organization can no longer be viewed as reliable.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:20.520
According to a letter made public Monday by
New York Attorney General Letitia James as

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:27.100
part of her civil probe into Trump's company,
Mazars also said it will no longer work with

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:31.350
the Trump Organization, meaning the company
may have to get new financial statements that

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:34.549
could complicate its ability to secure loans.

00:01:34.549 --> 00:01:40.610
In a Feb. nine letter from Mazars Group General
Counsel William Kelly to the Trump Organization's

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:46.610
chief legal officer, the auditing firm said
its work from 2011 to 2020 quote should not

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:49.200
be relied upon.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:55.790
In the world of corporate accounting, this
is like a groundbreaking statement of there's

00:01:55.790 --> 00:02:02.420
some really bad stuff going on here and we
meaning the accounting firm want to try to

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:06.200
get the hell out from under what might be
coming in our direction.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:12.290
They also added, We write to advise that the
statements of financial condition for Donald

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:19.280
J. Trump for the years ending June 30th, 2011
to June 30th, 2020, that's fiscal years should

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:21.260
no longer be relied upon.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:25.740
And you should inform any recipients thereof
currently relying upon one or more of those

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:28.510
documents that those documents should not
be relied upon.

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:34.400
Understand that that is a signal to all of
the lenders that have given Trump money on

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:37.190
the basis of these financial statements.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:43.140
They they're being told you made financial
decisions about the Trump Organization's credit

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:48.050
worthiness on the basis of account of account
accounting documents that we, the accounting

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:52.129
firm, are telling you cannot be relied upon.

00:02:52.129 --> 00:02:55.350
Here's a copy of the letter sent out.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:03:00.910
Dear Alan, this is to Alan Garten, the chief
legal officer of the Trump Organization and

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:02.349
from the accounting firm Dear Alan.

00:03:02.349 --> 00:03:04.290
It's like a Dear John letter.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:09.030
We write to advise that the statement a financial
condition for Donald J. Trump from 2011 to

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:13.560
2020, should no longer be relied upon, and
you should inform recipients relying on those

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.060
not to.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:16.440
We have come to this conclusion.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:17.760
This is the best part.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:21.010
We have come to this conclusion, based in
part upon the filings made by the New York

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:27.120
Attorney General on January 18th, 2020, to
our own investigation and information received

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:28.640
from internal and external sources.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:34.430
They are saying in part, the investigation
being carried out by Letitia James of New

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:43.450
York has brought to their attention the corruption
and alleged fraud potential fraud.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:48.739
I want to be careful with how I say that committed
by the Trump Organization and we already know

00:03:48.739 --> 00:03:53.489
what this relates to, this mostly seems to
relate to the valuation of assets.

00:03:53.489 --> 00:03:58.150
What Michael Cohen and others have told us
the Trump Organization would regularly do

00:03:58.150 --> 00:03:59.770
is you take a building.

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:05.450
Let's say we agree that in the real world,
the building is worth $20 million.

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:10.820
When it comes to assessment for tax purposes,
the Trump Organization would say, Look at

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:12.420
this crappy building.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:15.700
It's not worth 20 million, it's worth $10
million.

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:21.829
So tax us on the $10 million valuation and
they would submit documents supporting that.

00:04:21.829 --> 00:04:23.020
That's what it's worth.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:28.470
On the other hand, when the Trump Organization
wanted to get a loan using that same building

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:32.930
as collateral, they would say, wasn't this
building's not worth 10 million?

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:34.520
This building's not worth 20 million.

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:36.889
This building's worth $40 million.

00:04:36.889 --> 00:04:41.330
And so you can give us, you know, if it's
an 80 percent loan to value or whatever the

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:47.630
case is, you can give us a loan on the basis
that the collateral we're offering you is

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:50.650
worth 30 or $40 million rather than 20.

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:55.719
And that would encourage a lender to say we
can give them 28 million bucks because if

00:04:55.719 --> 00:05:00.360
they default, we take the building and we
sell the building for 30 or 40 when the building

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:06.620
is only worth 10 or 20, giving a $28 million
loan with that building as collateral obviously

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:11.430
is not a good idea for the lender, so that's
the gist of what has been done.

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:17.830
Other notes from the letter due in part to
our decision regarding the financial statements,

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:22.380
as well as the totality of the circumstances,
we have reached the point such that there

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:27.009
is a non-waiver ball conflict of interest
with the Trump Organization.

00:05:27.009 --> 00:05:35.899
As a result, we are not able to provide any
new work product to the Trump Organization.

00:05:35.899 --> 00:05:45.580
This is an example of rats abandoning a sinking
ship and its crimes all the way down, and

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:53.030
consider that Trump was elected partially
on the basis that he was a really successful

00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:54.839
entrepreneur.

00:05:54.839 --> 00:05:58.409
And then we found out, well, he's had a bunch
of business bankruptcies, but he said that

00:05:58.409 --> 00:06:01.809
was him just using the tax code to his advantage.

00:06:01.809 --> 00:06:08.449
This additional thing suggests that even the
degree to which his business was successful

00:06:08.449 --> 00:06:13.060
was based upon accounting distortions, or
at least potentially on that basis.

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:19.430
And when I hear you can't trust these accounting
documents and we're not working for you anymore,

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:25.550
what I hear is we committed fraud for the
boss and we're going to get caught and we're

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:27.869
doing what we can to wash our hands of him.

00:06:27.869 --> 00:06:31.969
And I think anybody who who knows anything
about Trump knows that cutting corners is

00:06:31.969 --> 00:06:33.050
sort of the name of the game.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:37.939
It's the status quo and people continue to
love the guy and defend the guy.

00:06:37.939 --> 00:06:43.089
But this is not looking good at all in terms
of this investigation into the Trump Organization.

00:06:43.089 --> 00:06:44.119
Will it ever hit Trump?

00:06:44.119 --> 00:06:45.429
I still don't think so.

00:06:45.429 --> 00:06:47.759
And I know many of you get mad when I say
that.

00:06:47.759 --> 00:06:48.759
But.

00:06:48.759 --> 00:06:49.759
I don't think so.

00:06:49.759 --> 00:07:55.430
Let me know if you have a different view on
that particular piece.

